    <!-- About -->
    <string name="about_title">About</string>
    <string name="about_tagline">Secure scanner, post-quantum verification</string>
    <string name="about_section_description">Description</string>
        <string name="about_description">BlokQR decodes QR codes and barcodes directly on your device, then analyzes their destination WITHOUT ever opening it. The target is inspected by a remote service that follows redirects and returns a signed verdict (safe, caution, dangerous or malicious), protecting you from phishing before any click. Offline, a bundled signed threat list takes over and blocks known malicious domains. Quick analysis is free (up to 7 checks per day); in-depth analysis (sandbox rendering and impersonation detection) is reserved for Pro subscribers.</string>
    <string name="about_section_features">Features</string>
    <string name="about_feature_airgap">Fully on-device decoding: the phone never opens the link itself.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_tiers">Same detection engine for everyone: reputation, redirects and security signals. Pro adds in-depth dynamic rendering.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_signed">Verdict authenticated by a hybrid signature (classical + post-quantum).</string>
    <string name="about_feature_sandbox">Built-in isolated browser to open a link safely.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_ai">Detection of brand impersonation and fraudulent login pages.</string>
    <string name="about_feature_privacy">Privacy: k-anonymity and no IP logging.</string>
    <string name="about_section_architecture">Technical architecture</string>
        <string name="about_architecture">Decoding runs on-device via ML Kit and recognises QR codes as well as the main 2D and barcode formats (Data Matrix, Aztec, PDF417, EAN, Code 128, etc.). The target is then sent to a stateless analysis service that follows redirects, queries reputation sources and performs sandboxed rendering. Each verdict is signed with a hybrid Ed25519 + ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) scheme and verified on-device; the SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s (FIPS 205) root of trust is pinned in the app and enables key rotation through a signed manifest. Communications are protected by TLS with certificate pinning, complemented by a hybrid X25519 + ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203) envelope that encrypts requests end-to-end up to the gateway. Interface available in 12 languages. Sovereign European hosting.</string>
    <string name="about_version">BlokQR v1.0.2</string>

