    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_updated">Last updated: June 2026</string>
    <string name="privacy_intro">BlokQR is built privacy-first. This page, bundled inside the app, explains what data is processed and why — no external connection is needed to read it.</string>
    <string name="privacy_s1_title">Local decoding</string>
    <string name="privacy_s1_body">When you scan a code, it is decoded locally on your device. The target page is never opened or loaded on your phone.</string>
    <string name="privacy_s2_title">Destination analysis</string>
        <string name="privacy_s2_body">To assess a link, its destination (the URL) is sent to our analysis service, which follows redirects and computes a verdict. Transport is protected by TLS and by a post-quantum X25519 + ML-KEM-768 envelope. This request is not tied to any identity.</string>
    <string name="privacy_s3_title">Camera</string>
    <string name="privacy_s3_body">The camera permission is used only to scan codes. Camera frames are processed locally for decoding: they are neither stored nor transmitted.</string>
    <string name="privacy_s4_title">Deep analysis (Pro)</string>
    <string name="privacy_s4_body">For in-depth analysis, our service produces a screenshot of the target page, rendered server-side, which is shown to you in the app. It is not shared with third parties.</string>
    <string name="privacy_s5_title">No identity, no tracking</string>
            <string name="privacy_s5_body">BlokQR creates no account and collects no personal identifier. Pro access relies on a signed bearer token that carries no personal data. No ads, no third-party trackers. Your scan history stays on your device, where it is encrypted, and you can clear it at any time or turn off recording.</string>
    <string name="privacy_s6_title">Subscriptions</string>
    <string name="privacy_s6_body">Subscriptions are handled by Google Play. Payment is processed by Google; we only verify that the purchase is valid. See Google\'s privacy policy for details.</string>
    <string name="privacy_s7_title">Security</string>
            <string name="privacy_s7_body">Communications use TLS with certificate pinning. Request contents are additionally encrypted end-to-end by a hybrid post-quantum X25519 + ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203) envelope. Verdicts are signed with a hybrid Ed25519 + ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) scheme and verified on your device to guarantee their authenticity and integrity. On your device, additional protections are available: your scan history is encrypted at rest (AES-256-GCM, with a non-exportable key held in the Android hardware-backed keystore); you can require biometrics to view this history and when BlokQR starts, using the phone sensor with fallback to the device lock code; you can also enable a secure screen that hides content in the app switcher and blocks screenshots. These locks remain entirely local: no account, no server, and biometrics never leave the phone’s secure module.</string>
    <string name="privacy_contact">Questions about your data? Email us at contact@blokqr.com.</string>
